# Blotter — credentials (Phase 0)
#
# HOW THIS FILE IS USED
#   Bitget's own tools deliberately do NOT read .env files, so this file is a
#   staging area, not a runtime input for them. Our scripts load it explicitly:
#       node --import ./scripts/load-env.mjs --import ./scripts/doh-preload.mjs <script>
#   and for Bitget tools we export from it first:
#       set -a && . ./.env && set +a && bgc ...
#
# SAFETY
#   - .env is gitignored; only .env.example is committed. Never paste real keys
#     into an issue, a commit, a screenshot, or the demo video.
#   - The read-only key is used LOCALLY only. The hosted app never asks for keys.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spike A + Bitget path — REAL account, READ-ONLY
#   Create at: https://www.bitget.com/en/api-management  (Settings → API Management)
#   Tick: Read-only. Do NOT tick Trade or Transfer for this key.
#   Copy all three values: Key, Secret Key, Passphrase (set at creation).
#   ▸ Which account: the one holding the stock-perp trades you want reviewed.
#     For the hero demo I need >= 30 closed trips in the last 90 days.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BITGET_API_KEY=
BITGET_SECRET_KEY=
BITGET_PASSPHRASE=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spike D — Bitget DEMO (paper trading) key, separate from the key above
#   Same page, but switch the API-key page to "Demo Trading" / paper environment
#   first: https://www.bitget.com/en/api-management
#   Tick Trade (paper trading needs write access to the demo books).
#   ▸ Used ONLY for the on-camera "BLOCKED by R-03" proof on paper trading.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BITGET_DEMO_API_KEY=
BITGET_DEMO_SECRET_KEY=
BITGET_DEMO_PASSPHRASE=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spike E + Phase 5 — LLM providers (the desk)
#   Claude: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys  (starts with sk-ant-)
#   Qwen (Bitget hackathon endpoint): credits via the official Telegram
#     https://hackathon.bitgetops.com/v1  — key supplied after their KYC/application.
#     The CLI expects it as BITGET_QWEN_API_KEY (main2.md:571).
#   Either one is enough to finish Spike E; both is better (provider fallback).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
BITGET_QWEN_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional overrides (defaults are fine)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BITGET_API_BASE_URL=https://api.bitget.com
# BITGET_DOH_URL=https://cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query
# BITGET_MCP_URL=https://agent.bitget.com/mcp
